<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The capabilities of pi² for iPhone (docs/iphone.md 3.2, 6.4, 9.1; #682). Xcode signs the app with this file in
     both configurations (CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in iphone/pi2.xcodeproj), and every capability here is one the App ID
     `dev.pi2.ios` must have in Apple's developer site before a build for a phone signs: docs/releasing.md, "The iPhone
     app and TestFlight", has the owner's steps.

     - aps-environment: the relay's pushes (section 7). A development build is signed for `development`; a TestFlight
       build is signed with the distribution profile, whose `production` value Xcode puts here in place of this one.
     - com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment: App Attest, which pairing proves the app with (3.2, 3.3).
       Apple attests only for the environment a build was signed for, so it is `development` in a Debug build and
       `production` in a Release one, as PI2_APP_ATTEST_ENVIRONMENT says in the project.
     - com.apple.security.application-groups: the group the app and its three extensions read (`AppGroup.id`). Without
       it, `containerURL(forSecurityApplicationGroupIdentifier:)` is nil in each of them.
     - keychain-access-groups: the group the record key and what the phone keeps of the Mac are in, which the
       notification service extension reads to open a push that arrives while the phone is locked (3.2). Only the items
       marked `shared` (`KeyItem.shared`) go there; the phone's other keys stay in the app's own group, which the
       extension cannot read. `PI2KeychainAccessGroup` in Info.plist is the same group as the app names it at runtime,
       since only the build knows the team's prefix. -->
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment</key>
	<string>$(PI2_APP_ATTEST_ENVIRONMENT)</string>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.dev.pi2.ios</string>
	</array>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)group.dev.pi2.ios</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
